The `dequeueMatching` method in `FlowFnQueueAdapter` will never work because it calls `this.peek(queueName)` which always returns an empty array `[]` (line 113-115). This means the for loop will never execute and the method will always return `null`, even if matching items exist in the queue.

This is a critical bug that breaks the functionality of `dequeueMatching` for the FlowFn adapter. Either:
1. Implement `peek` to make an API call to retrieve queued items, or
2. Document that `dequeueMatching` is not supported for FlowFn and throw an error:

```typescript
async dequeueMatching(queueName: string, matcher: (payload: TPayload) => boolean): Promise<TPayload | null> {
  throw new Error('dequeueMatching is not supported for FlowFnQueueAdapter');
}
